 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# `indic/04` — Tokenization Parity (TP)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Compute Tokenization Parity (TP) — a measure of how much more the\n",
    "XLM-RoBERTa tokenizer fragments Indic-script text compared to English.\n",
    "TP is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{TP}(L) = \\frac{|t(s_L)|}{|t(s_E)|}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $t(\\cdot)$ is the XLM-RoBERTa subword tokenizer and $s_E$ is the\n",
    "English source sentence. TP = 1.0 means identical token count to English;\n",
    "TP > 1.0 indicates over-fragmentation.\n",
    "\n",
    "TP is computed for both **native-script** and **romanised** conditions\n",
    "on the hypothesis (translation) column, mirroring the two experimental\n",
    "conditions used in the analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reads:** `data/indic/<ISO>_indicmt.csv` (produced by `indic/01` and `indic/02`)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:** Adds columns `tp_nat` and `tp_rom` to each per-language CSV.\n",
    "A cross-language summary table is printed at the end.\n",
    "\n",
    "**TP interpretation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| TP value | Interpretation |\n",
    "|----------|----------------|\n",
    "| 1.0 | Same token count as English — no tokenizer overhead |\n",
    "| 1.5 | 50% more tokens than English — moderate fragmentation |\n",
    "| 2.0 | 100% more tokens than English — high fragmentation |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**References**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Petrov, A., La Malfa, E., Torr, P. H. S., & Bibi, A. (2023). Language model\n",
    "  tokenizers introduce unfairness between languages. *NeurIPS 2023*, vol. 36.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Kanjirangat, V., Samardžić, T., Dolamic, L., & Rinaldi, F. (2025).\n",
    "  Tokenization and representation biases in multilingual models on dialectal\n",
    "  NLP tasks. *EMNLP 2025*, pp. 23992–24010.\n",
    "  https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.20045\n",
    "\n",
    "- Conneau, A., et al. (2020). Unsupervised cross-lingual representation\n",
    "  learning at scale. *ACL 2020*, pp. 8440–8451.\n",
    "  https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.02116\n",
    "\n",
    "- Rei, R., Stewart, C., Farinha, A. C., & Lavie, A. (2020). COMET: A Neural\n",
    "  Framework for MT Evaluation. *EMNLP 2020*, pp. 2685–2702.\n",
    "  https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.213\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sai B., A., et al. (2023). IndicMT Eval: A Dataset to Meta-Evaluate Machine\n",
    "  Translation Metrics for Indian Languages. *ACL 2023*, pp. 14210–14228.\n",
    "  https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.795"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "install_deps",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import subprocess, sys\n",
    "\n",
    "def _install(pkg):\n",
    "    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', pkg, '-q'])\n",
    "\n",
    "for pkg in ['transformers', 'pandas']:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        __import__(pkg)\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        print(f'Installing {pkg}...'); _install(pkg)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dependencies ready.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_config",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "All paths are relative to the repository root.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `DATA_DIR` — directory containing the five per-language CSVs from `indic/01`/`indic/02`\n",
    "- `HYP_COL` — column name for the machine translation hypothesis (native script)\n",
    "- `HYP_ROM_COL` — column name for the romanised hypothesis (added by `indic/02`)\n",
    "- `SRC_COL` — column name for the English source (denominator of TP)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "config",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path('data/indic')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Column names ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "SRC_COL     = 'src'       # English source sentence\n",
    "HYP_COL     = 'hyp'       # native-script hypothesis\n",
    "HYP_ROM_COL = 'hyp_rom'   # romanised hypothesis (from indic/02)\n",
    "REF_COL     = 'ref'       # native-script reference\n",
    "REF_ROM_COL = 'ref_rom'   # romanised reference (from indic/02)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Language config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "LANGUAGES = ['GUJ', 'HIN', 'MAL', 'MAR', 'TAM']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Data directory : {DATA_DIR.resolve()}')\n",
    "print(f'Languages      : {LANGUAGES}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_tokenizer",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Load XLM-RoBERTa Tokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `xlm-roberta-base`, which is the backbone tokenizer of\n",
    "`Unbabel/wmt22-comet-da` (unbabel-comet 2.2.6). Token counts from this\n",
    "tokenizer are used as $|t(\\cdot)|$ in the TP formula.\n",
    "\n",
    "The first run will download the tokenizer vocabulary (~1 MB). Subsequent\n",
    "runs use the Hugging Face cache."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "load_tokenizer",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "from transformers import XLMRobertaTokenizerFast\n",
    "\n",
    "TOKENIZER_NAME = 'xlm-roberta-base'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loading tokenizer: {TOKENIZER_NAME}')\n",
    "tokenizer = XLMRobertaTokenizerFast.from_pretrained(TOKENIZER_NAME)\n",
    "print('Tokenizer loaded.\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def token_count(text: str) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return the number of XLM-R subword tokens for a single string.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if not text or (isinstance(text, float) and pd.isna(text)):\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    return len(tokenizer.tokenize(str(text)))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_load",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Load Per-Language CSVs\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the five CSVs written by `indic/01` and `indic/02`. Confirm that\n",
    "`src`, `hyp`, `ref`, `hyp_rom`, and `ref_rom` are all present before\n",
    "computing token counts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "load_csvs",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "data = {}  # iso -> pd.DataFrame\n",
    "\n",
    "REQUIRED = [SRC_COL, HYP_COL, REF_COL, HYP_ROM_COL, REF_ROM_COL]\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso in LANGUAGES:\n",
    "    path = DATA_DIR / f'{iso}_indicmt.csv'\n",
    "    if not path.exists():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "            f'{path} not found. Run indic/01 and indic/02 first.')\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
    "    data[iso] = df\n",
    "\n",
    "    present = [c for c in REQUIRED if c in df.columns]\n",
    "    missing = [c for c in REQUIRED if c not in df.columns]\n",
    "    status  = 'OK' if not missing else f'MISSING: {missing}'\n",
    "    print(f'  {iso}  {len(df):,} rows  |  required cols: {status}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nLoaded {len(data)} language files.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_tp",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Compute Token Counts and TP\n",
    "\n",
    "For each sentence we compute:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `src_tc` — XLM-R token count of the English source (denominator)\n",
    "2. `hyp_tc` — token count of the native-script hypothesis\n",
    "3. `hyp_rom_tc` — token count of the romanised hypothesis\n",
    "4. `ref_tc` — token count of the native-script reference\n",
    "5. `ref_rom_tc` — token count of the romanised reference\n",
    "\n",
    "TP ratios are then:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{tp\_nat} = \\frac{\\text{hyp\_tc}}{\\text{src\_tc}}, \\quad\n",
    "\\text{tp\_rom} = \\frac{\\text{hyp\_rom\_tc}}{\\text{src\_tc}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Division by zero is avoided by replacing zero English token counts with NaN.\n",
    "If TP columns already exist in a CSV (from a previous run), they are\n",
    "recomputed and overwritten to ensure consistency."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "compute_tp",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Column definitions: (output_tc_col, output_tp_col, text_col, use_as_denominator)\n",
    "TC_SPEC = [\n",
    "    ('src_tc',         None,       SRC_COL,     True),\n",
    "    ('hyp_tc',         'tp_nat',   HYP_COL,     False),\n",
    "    ('ref_tc',         'tp_ref',   REF_COL,     False),\n",
    "    ('hyp_rom_tc',     'tp_rom',   HYP_ROM_COL, False),\n",
    "    ('ref_rom_tc',     'tp_ref_rom', REF_ROM_COL, False),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "summary_rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{'='*55}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{iso} — Tokenization Parity\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{'='*55}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # compute English source token counts (denominator)\n",
    "    if SRC_COL in df.columns:\n",
    "        df['src_tc'] = df[SRC_COL].apply(token_count)\n",
    "        src_tc = df['src_tc'].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Column '{SRC_COL}' not found in {iso}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    for tc_col, tp_col, text_col, is_denom in TC_SPEC:\n",
    "        if is_denom:\n",
    "            continue  # already done above\n",
    "        if text_col not in df.columns:\n",
    "            print(f\"  '{text_col}' not in {iso} — skipped\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "\n",
    "        df[tc_col] = df[text_col].apply(token_count)\n",
    "        df[tp_col] = df[tc_col] / src_tc\n",
    "\n",
    "        mean_tp = df[tp_col].mean()\n",
    "        print(f\"  {tp_col:<14}  mean = {mean_tp:.3f}  \"",
    "              f\"(token count: min={df[tc_col].min()}, mean={df[tc_col].mean():.1f}, max={df[tc_col].max()})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        summary_rows.append({'Language': iso, 'Column': text_col,\n",
    "                              'TP_col': tp_col, 'Mean_TP': round(mean_tp, 4)})\n",
    "\n",
    "    data[iso] = df\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_tp_inv",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — TP–IP Inversion Check\n",
    "\n",
    "Under romanisation, TP is expected to **inflate** for every Indic language\n",
    "(more tokens needed because Latin-script Indic digrams are absent from\n",
    "the XLM-R vocabulary and are split into single characters).\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell computes the per-language TP delta\n",
    "$\\Delta\\text{TP} = \\text{tp\_rom} - \\text{tp\_nat}$ and confirms the direction\n",
    "is positive for all five languages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "tp_inversion",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "print(f\"{'Lang':6s}  {'TP_nat':>8s}  {'TP_rom':>8s}  {'Delta_TP':>10s}  {'Delta%':>8s}\")\n",
    "print('-' * 50)\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    if 'tp_nat' not in df.columns or 'tp_rom' not in df.columns:\n",
    "        print(f'  {iso}  — tp_nat or tp_rom missing, skipped')\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    tp_nat  = df['tp_nat'].mean()\n",
    "    tp_rom  = df['tp_rom'].mean()\n",
    "    delta   = tp_rom - tp_nat\n",
    "    pct     = (delta / tp_nat) * 100\n",
    "    arrow   = '↑' if delta > 0 else '↓'\n",
    "    print(f'  {iso:4s}  {tp_nat:>8.3f}  {tp_rom:>8.3f}  {arrow}{delta:>9.3f}  {pct:>+7.1f}%')\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Expected: Delta_TP > 0 (TP inflates) for all five languages under romanisation.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_save",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — Save Updated CSVs\n",
    "\n",
    "Write the updated DataFrames (with token-count and TP columns) back to\n",
    "`data/indic/`. Downstream notebooks (`indic/05` onwards) read these files."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "save_csvs",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "TP_COLS = ['src_tc', 'hyp_tc', 'ref_tc', 'hyp_rom_tc', 'ref_rom_tc',\n",
    "           'tp_nat', 'tp_ref', 'tp_rom', 'tp_ref_rom']\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    out_path = DATA_DIR / f'{iso}_indicmt.csv'\n",
    "    df.to_csv(out_path, index=False)\n",
    "    present = [c for c in TP_COLS if c in df.columns]\n",
    "    print(f'  Saved  {out_path}  ({len(df):,} rows)  TP cols: {present}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\n  {len(data)} files updated in {DATA_DIR.resolve()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Cross-Language TP Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Print the mean native-script and romanised TP for every language.\n",
    "These values correspond to the `TP_nat` column in the master language\n",
    "profile table and to Figure 1 (right panel — TP inflates under romanisation)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "summary_table",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "print(f\"{'Lang':6s}  {'TP_nat':>8s}  {'TP_ref':>8s}  {'TP_rom':>8s}  {'TP_ref_rom':>11s}\")\n",
    "print('-' * 55)\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    vals = {}\n",
    "    for col in ['tp_nat', 'tp_ref', 'tp_rom', 'tp_ref_rom']:\n",
    "        vals[col] = f\"{df[col].mean():.3f}\" if col in df.columns else '--'\n",
    "    print(f\"  {iso:4s}  {vals['tp_nat']:>8s}  {vals['tp_ref']:>8s}  \"",
    "          f\"{vals['tp_rom']:>8s}  {vals['tp_ref_rom']:>11s}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('TP > 1.0 indicates over-fragmentation relative to English.')\n",
    "print('tp_nat : native-script hypothesis TP')\n",
    "print('tp_ref : native-script reference TP')\n",
    "print('tp_rom : romanised hypothesis TP (should exceed tp_nat)')\n",
    "print('tp_ref_rom : romanised reference TP')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('data/indic/ is ready for indic/05 (Information Parity computation).')"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
